CODEGEN.md §3.5, §5.2, DECISIONS 383: a closed @codes enum's detail::<E>Ordinal, detail::k<E>Codes and detail::k<E>CodeOrdinals go through the C++ name plan, so a record named like the ordinal (which detail's name would hide) is E8005, not a header g++ misreads.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// An element.
enum Element @codes(UInt8) { FIRE = 1, WATER = 2 }

/// Named like the ordinal.
record ElementOrdinal {
  /// Its value.
  v: Int
}

emit cpp { out: "@features/a/cpp", namespace: "a", mode: types }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8005]  a/a.canon:7:8
  cpp: ElementOrdinal is generated for both a.ElementOrdinal and a.Element; rename one of them with @cpp(name:)

